# These upstream files mix supported CallTracker semantics with §13
# metaobject requirements. The supported portions remain under local/.
test-assert-calltracker-calls.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires Proxy-transparent callback identity plus observable and mutable function length/custom-property metadata; supported forwarding, return, validation, and counting are retained in local/calltracker-static.js
test-assert-calltracker-getCalls.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires Object.freeze non-extensibility for the returned list, records, and argument arrays; supported call snapshots and reset semantics are retained in local/calltracker-static.js
test-assert-calltracker-report.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); its only assertions require copying the wrapped function's observable name into diagnostics; static diagnostics use the stable operation name and are covered in local/calltracker-static.js
test-assert-calltracker-verify.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); every asserted diagnostic depends on the wrapped functions' observable names; supported aggregate and single failure behavior is retained in local/calltracker-static.js
test-assert-checktag.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); the test constructs fake Date, global, and process objects by reading and replacing prototype chains, and its subject is detection of those forgeries
test-assert-esm-cjs-message-verify.js: harness isolation; every assertion is about fresh child Node processes which load Node's built-in assert module, so the result is unchanged when our module is sabotaged
test-assert-first-line.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires V8 structured stack/source locations to recover and print the exact expression text from a separately loaded fixture
test-assert-if-error.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); irreducibly requires exact V8 stack-frame splicing and function-name elision; supported value, message, and AssertionError fields are retained in local/if-error-static.js
test-assert-async.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); irreducibly asserts callback-name-dependent diagnostics and exact V8 stack-frame elision; supported Promise, function, thenable, expectation, and pass-through behavior is retained in local/async-static.js
test-assert.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); this broad file irreducibly mixes VM realms, arbitrary discovered error-property bags, prototype constructors, source-expression recovery, custom inspect symbols, and observable function/stack metadata; supported core assertions and closed error fields are retained in local/core-static.js
test-assert-deep-with-error.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); after cause comparison succeeds, every assertion requires a prototype-preserving Error copy with hidden property descriptors solely for V8's exact diagnostic rendering; supported cause equality is retained in local/deep-error-static.js
